# SET VlE
# Seq 21. 26. 4 M
# 1 of 1
# Fix to SET TTY NO SCOPE support.
# Problem:   SET TTY NO SCOPE breaks expected behavior with rubouts
# in the Keyboard Monitor such that it doesn't properly prefix
# the string of deleted chars with a backslash.
# Diagnosis:  In V3F the location of page zero literals shifted.
# When restoring NO SCOPE the wrong location for ['\ is used.
# Solution:  Install the following patch:
.GET SYS:SET
.ODT
0507/6105 6106
3254/1070 1101
\c
.SAVE SYS:SET
# This patch upgrades SET to Version VIF.
# NO SCOPE rubout processing will again prefix
# the echoed string of characters with a backslash.
# Note this is not an official DEC SPR, but 
# OS/8 v3f isn't official either.